#X text 82 4396 One 4-pole VCF for the instrument (NJM2069) and one DEG3 for all voices \, measured on a Poly-800 II. \; cut (99): 0-99 = 66 Hz - 20 kHz \, 13 steps per octave. \; res (0): 0-15 \, an uncompensated ladder (the bass falls as it rises) \, no self-oscillation. \; kbd (0): key tracking of the highest key: 0 off \, 2 full (1:1 \, C4 nominal) \, 1 half (1:2 \, C6 nominal). \; egi (0): EG INT 0-15 \, DEG3 moves the cutoff up to 7.9 octaves. \; pol (2): 2 up \, 1 down. \; trg (2): 2 multi: every key restarts DEG3 \, 1 single: only the first key of a phrase. \; env3 (0): DEG3 morph as env1 (see Controls) \, -1 = own values. \; a3 d3 bp3 sl3 su3 r3: attack \, decay \, break point \, slope \, sustain \, release of DEG3 \, 0-31. \; nois (0): white noise 0-15 \, its VCA follows DEG3. \; drv (0): overdrive (not on the Poly-800) \, soft clipping \, 0-127 = 0-48 dB more gain with level makeup. \; drvp (0): 0 post: after the VCF \, denser with res and chords \, 1 pre: into the VCF \, which rounds the distortion off (warmer). \; vcut (0): velocity to the cutoff: at 127 a soft key is up to 5 octaves lower \, full velocity plays the cut set (one VCF: the last key counts)., f 64;
